<h2 class="wp-block-heading">What is link building?</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading --></div>
<!-- /wp:column -->

<!-- wp:column {"width":"60%"} -->
<div class="wp-block-column" style="flex-basis:60%"><!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A link is a clickable reference from one website to another. Google treats links a little like recommendations: if trusted sites point to yours, your pages are more likely to be shown. Link building is the work of earning or placing those references.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>There are two useful kinds for a small business. Profile and citation links are your business details on directories and platforms. They are simple, low-risk and help Google confirm who you are. Guest posts are articles published on other websites with a link back to you. They carry more weight, and the weight depends on the site.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You will see "DR" on the premium packages. DR means Domain Rating, a score from 0 to 100 made by the tool Ahrefs to estimate how strong a website's own links are. It is not a Google number, but it is a fair shorthand: a link from a DR 50 site is harder to get, and usually worth more, than one from a DR 10 site.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>
<!-- /wp:column --></div>
<!-- /wp:columns --></section>
<!-- /wp:group -->

