<!-- wp:group {"className":"ifm-faq","layout":{"type":"constrained"}} -->
<div class="wp-block-group ifm-faq"><!-- wp:details -->
<details class="wp-block-details"><summary>Are these links safe?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>We place links on real, established sites and directories, by hand. We do not use private blog networks, hacked sites or bulk tools, which are the methods Google penalises. No link is risk-free for ever, because publishers can change their sites.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details -->

<!-- wp:details -->
<details class="wp-block-details"><summary>Will the links be "dofollow"?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Each site decides how it marks its links, and many label paid placements as sponsored, as Google asks them to. We do not promise a type. We tell you what each link is in the report.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details -->

<!-- wp:details -->
<details class="wp-block-details"><summary>What happens if a link disappears?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A link that is not live at delivery is replaced free. Guest posts removed within 90 days are also replaced. The exact terms are on each package.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details -->

<!-- wp:details -->
<details class="wp-block-details"><summary>Which DR should I choose?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Start one step above where your own site is. A new site gains from DR 20 to 30 links. Going straight to DR 70 costs more and can look unnatural beside a thin link profile.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details -->

<!-- wp:details -->
<details class="wp-block-details"><summary>Can I approve the sites first?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>For guest posts, yes. Tell us in the order form and we send the proposed site before publishing.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
